.Dd July 9, 2026
.Dt MAC-POLICY 5
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac-policy
.Nd MAC policy configuration file format
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file format is used by the MAC (Mandatory Access Control) framework
in GergiOS to define access control rules. The policy is loaded by
the
.Xr macd 8
daemon at startup and can be reloaded via SIGHUP.
.Pp
Policy files reside in
.Pa /etc/macd.conf
(text format) or optionally
.Pa /etc/macd.policy
(compiled binary format, see
.Xr mac-compile 8 ) .
.Sh SYNTAX
Policy files use a simple line-based syntax:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Sy Comments
Lines starting with
.Ql #
are comments and are ignored.
.It Sy Allow ALL
.Pp
.Dl allow ALL;
.Pp
Disables MAC enforcement (compat mode). All operations are permitted.
.It Sy Allow/Deny rules
.Pp
.Dl allow OPERATION from SOURCE to TARGET;
.Dl deny OPERATION from SOURCE to TARGET;
.El
.Sh OPERATIONS
The following operation types are supported:
.Bl -tag -width PRIVCTL_SET_SYS
.It Sy IPC_SEND
IPC message send between processes.
.It Sy PRIVCTL_SET_SYS
Privilege level change via
.Xr sys_privctl 2 .
.It Sy PROC_FORK
Process fork.
.It Sy PROC_EXEC
Process exec.
.It Sy PROC_KILL
Process signal delivery.
.It Sy FILE_ACCESS
File open/read/write access.
.It Sy DEVICE_BIND
Device bind/unbind.
.It Sy RAWIO
Raw I/O port access.
.It Sy ALL
Matches any operation type.
.El
.Sh SOURCE AND TARGET
Source and target are endpoint labels. The following forms are accepted:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Sy any
Matches any process endpoint.
.It Sy self
Matches the calling process.
.It Sy label
A service label from
.Pa /etc/system.conf
(e.g.,
.Ic pm ,
.Ic vfs ,
.Ic rs ) .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/macd.policy -compact
.It Pa /etc/macd.conf
Default MAC policy configuration file (text format).
.It Pa /etc/macd.policy
Optional compiled MAC policy (binary format).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Compat mode (MAC disabled)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Allow everything (MAC disabled)
allow ALL;
.Ed
.Ss Strict per-service policy
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Core services
allow IPC_SEND from pm to vfs;
allow IPC_SEND from pm to vm;
allow IPC_SEND from pm to ds;
allow PRIVCTL_SET_SYS from rs to any;
allow PROC_KILL from pm to any;
allow PROC_FORK from pm to any;
allow PROC_EXEC from pm to any;

# Filesystem access
allow FILE_ACCESS from vfs to mfs;
allow FILE_ACCESS from vfs to ext4;
allow FILE_ACCESS from vfs to ext2;

# Device binding
allow DEVICE_BIND from rs to devman;
allow DEVICE_BIND from devman to ahci;
allow DEVICE_BIND from devman to virtio_blk;

# Default deny (implicit)
.Ed
.Ss Compile policy for better performance
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ mac-compile -o /etc/macd.policy /etc/macd.conf
$ kill -HUP $(cat /var/run/macd.pid)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr macd 8 ,
.Xr mac-compile 8 ,
.Xr macctl 8 ,
.Xr system.conf 5 ,
.Xr auditd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The GergiOS MAC framework first appeared in GergiOS 1.0.
